# Navigation (React SPA)

## Primary chrome

- **Desktop:** left sidebar ([`resources/js/components/Sidebar.tsx`](resources/js/components/Sidebar.tsx)) driven by [`config/navigation.ts`](resources/js/config/navigation.ts) (e.g. Game lobby, My sessions). The app root `/` redirects to **`/game-sessions/lobby`**.
- **Mobile:** [`Header.tsx`](resources/js/components/Header.tsx) + slide-out drawer with the same nav items.
- **Profile / admin:** [`UserActions.tsx`](resources/js/components/UserActions.tsx) at the bottom of the sidebar (and mobile drawer): Profile link, Sign out, appearance toggle, compact sidebar control; **Admin Panel** (`/admin`) for admins only. These are not entries in `navigationSections`.

## Page layout

- Prefer [`PageShell`](resources/js/components/layout/PageShell.tsx) + [`PageHeader`](resources/js/components/layout/PageHeader.tsx) for new or refactored screens (max width, padding, single `<h1>` in the header). Use [`Surface`](resources/js/components/layout/Surface.tsx) for optional grouping (`tint` / `elevated`) instead of ad hoc `bg-card` + `shadow-md` stacks. Auth and global error states use [`AuthPageFrame`](resources/js/components/layout/AuthPageFrame.tsx) + `Surface` elevated. Legacy pages may still use `container mx-auto …` until migrated.
- Use **one top-level `<h1>`** per screen; keep hierarchy consistent with surrounding pages.
- Prefer **`Link`** (or `Button` / `ButtonLink` to a known route) for “back” and parent navigation. **Do not use `navigate(-1)`** for primary navigation so deep links and bookmarks stay predictable.
- If you later introduce route `location.state` for return paths, pass it through links explicitly rather than relying on history.

## Secondary actions

- Place primary actions for the screen in the header row next to the title (see Game lobby page) or in context-appropriate positions; reuse `@/components/ui/Button` and `ButtonLink`.

## Tabs

- If you add section tabs, use **`NavLink`** (or the same pattern as elsewhere in the app) and keep spacing consistent with sibling content (e.g. margin below the tab row when needed).
